  "seven_q": {
    "Q0_posture": "This document takes a confident, analytical posture, presenting a structural isomorphism as a proven claim with falsification criteria.",
    "Q1_identity": "A formal isomorphism paper establishing a structural mapping between the Born Rule and the Trinity.",
    "Q2_domain": "Intersection of quantum physics, trinitarian theology, and mathematics.",
    "Q3_claim": "The Born Rule's three irreducible operations (|\u03c8\u27e9, \u27e8\u03c6|, |\u00b7|\u00b2) map structurally to the three Persons of the Trinity (Father, Son, Spirit) with consistent roles across six biblical events.",
    "Q4_support": "Six biblical events tested with zero role violations; mathematical irreducibility of Born Rule; anti-modalism test; non-arbitrariness test; bidirectionality test.",
    "Q5_dependencies": "Depends on the Born Rule as fundamental quantum law; depends on orthodox trinitarian theology; depends on six specific biblical events being correctly interpreted.",
    "Q6_consequences": "Forces a triune structure in fundamental physics; forces quantum measurement to require three irreducible agents; provides a bridge between physics and theology.",
    "Q7_kill": "Seven kill conditions: wrong Born Rule operation in any event; Born Rule reducible to fewer operations; non-Trinitarian theology produces same mapping; Spirit not actualizing; Father actively selecting; Son not structuring; any tested event fails."
  },
